# tally 2.1.8 S6 (#187), L §6.1 l.1805: same is an equivalence, lines that share a side make one class. x[a] = y[a]
# (version one) and y[b] = y[a] (version two, known later) join x[a], y[a] and y[b]; they state 2, 3 and 4: every read
# of the class is one HOLE-SAME naming each row and value, in id order (L §8.1). x[b] = y[c] and x[c] = y[c] join a
# class that states 5 twice and x[b] nothing: 5. Before version two is known, y[b] is no side (4) and x[a] the pair's
# hole. 2.1.7's refcore kept each row's last partner only (y[b] read y[a] alone, x[a] read x[a] and y[a]).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
kind persons
input x[p in persons]: int
input y[p in persons]: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [a] lives 2026-01-01..
  persons + [b] lives 2026-01-01..
  persons + [c] lives 2026-01-01..
  x[a] = 2 "s"
  y[a] = 3 "s"
  y[b] = 4 "s"
  x[c] = 5 "s"
  y[c] = 5 "s"

version one
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-02
  same x[a] = y[a]
  same x[c] = y[c]

version two
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-03
  same y[b] = y[a]
  same x[b] = y[c]

ask xa: x[a]
ask yb: y[b]
ask xb: x[b]
ask yc: y[c]
ask yb2: y[b] as known 2026-01-02
ask xa2: x[a] as known 2026-01-02
=== expect
xa: ?"x[a], y[a] and y[b] are one, but the value differs on every day: 2 (v:x[a]), 3 (v:y[a]) and 4 (v:y[b])" (x[a], y[a], y[b])
  cut 2026-03-01
xa2: ?"x[a] and y[a] are one, but the value differs on every day: 2 (v:x[a]) and 3 (v:y[a])" (x[a], y[a])
  cut 2026-01-02
xb: 5
  cut 2026-03-01
yb: ?"x[a], y[a] and y[b] are one, but the value differs on every day: 2 (v:x[a]), 3 (v:y[a]) and 4 (v:y[b])" (x[a], y[a], y[b])
  cut 2026-03-01
yb2: 4
  cut 2026-01-02
yc: 5
  cut 2026-03-01
